      "writtenOn": "2023-06-08T14:49:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My perception was that `ShouldKeepExistingBuildFileForDir` is not actually that cheap a call (because it has to do a lot of recursive-directory path logic in the worst case)\n\nThrough experimentation I can\u0027t find any reliable difference between having this call last or having it first.\n\nHowever, you may be right that Stat should in general be a slower call (File I/O is usually the bottleneck!), and it\u0027s also easier to optimize an allowlist lookup.\n\nGood observation :)",
